\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Swept map seed 1, superlattice placement tiles, as one pass reports it. Left: $Z=(9,15)$ forces the seats $(8,15)$ and $(7,16)$, which are diagonal neighbours (red); $(11,15)$ (also outlined) forces $(9,15)$'s cells and runs into the same pair. Right: $(9,11)$ is refuted only through its n-ary facts; its chain up to the first contradiction has 8 cells and two blocking pairs.}}{1}{figure.caption.1}\protected@file@percent }
